CORE wide-pointer-encoding
main-violation.c
--wide-pointer-encoding
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ expected to FAIL: p->q can equal &x: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Violation direction of the pointer-containing-object dispatch case: asserting
p->q != &x must FAIL, confirming the skipped candidate is still resolved and
the solver does not miss the model (no unsound "no target").
